{
  "uid": "infrastructure",
  "title": "Infrastructure",
  "description": "The machine and the containers on it. Request rates, ticks and alerts live on the Crypto Alerts dashboard; this one answers why a container restarted.",
  "tags": [
    "crypto-alerts",
    "infrastructure"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "container",
        "label": "Container",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "definition": "label_values(container_memory_rss{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}, name)",
        "query": "label_values(container_memory_rss{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}, name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {},
        "options": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Containers",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Memory against its limit",
      "description": "How full each container's cgroup is. Under cgroup v2 anonymous memory, page cache and slab are all charged against the same ceiling, so this is the number the kernel acts on — not the process RSS. Containers with no limit report a limit of 0 and are filtered out rather than drawn as infinity, which is why this panel is empty on a laptop and populated in production.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 75
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "expr": "100 * container_memory_usage_bytes{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} / (container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory breakdown — $container",
      "description": "The panel ticket 09 needed and did not have. `docker stats` adds these three together and reports the sum, which is how a flat process looked like a leaking one: the growth was the kernel's reclaimable dentry cache, charged to the cgroup but belonging to no process. Anonymous is what a kill is decided on; page cache and slab are reclaimed first.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "bytes",
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 25,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "limit"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.stacking",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "none"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineStyle",
                "value": {
                  "fill": "dash",
                  "dash": [
                    10,
                    10
                  ]
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_rss{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "anonymous"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_cache{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "page cache"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_memory_kernel_usage{name=\"$container\"}",
          "legendFormat": "kernel / slab"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_spec_memory_limit_bytes{name=\"$container\"} > 0",
          "legendFormat": "limit"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Restarts and kills",
      "description": "Plain Docker has no restart counter, so a restart is read as a step change in the container's start time — `changes()` over the last hour counts them. Beside it, two independent witnesses to an OOM kill: cAdvisor's per-container event, and the kernel's own global counter through node-exporter. Before this panel existed, both were only visible in `journalctl -k` behind sudo.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "changes(container_start_time_seconds{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}} restarts"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "increase(container_oom_events_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[1h]) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}} OOM"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "increase(node_vmstat_oom_kill[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "host OOM kills"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Healthcheck state",
      "description": "What each container's own probe currently reports. Containers without a healthcheck report -1 and are filtered out. This is the piece that turns a restart into a story: a probe that had been failing for minutes before the restart says something different from one that was healthy right up to the kill.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 1
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "1": {
                  "text": "healthy",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "0": {
                  "text": "unhealthy",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false,
          "expr": "container_health_state{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} != -1",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU",
      "description": "Cores consumed per container, and where a ceiling exists, the ceiling. The host has two vCPUs, so the sum of these against 2 is the honest measure of how much room is left. Only the telemetry services are capped; the application services are deliberately uncapped.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisLabel": "cores"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[5m])",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "container_spec_cpu_quota{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"} / container_spec_cpu_period{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}} limit"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Reclaim forced at the ceiling",
      "description": "cgroup v2's memory.events \"max\" counter: how many times the kernel had to reclaim because a container hit its limit. Nothing dies, so this is invisible in restarts and in `docker inspect` — and it is exactly what the API container was doing 160 times in two days while its `docker stats` figure sat at 96.7% of the limit. A container that is quietly reclaiming at its boundary is fine right up until the moment it is not.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "increase(container_memory_events_max_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[1h]) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory pressure (PSI)",
      "description": "The fraction of wall-clock time in which every task in the container was stalled waiting for memory. This is the kernel's own verdict on whether a container is struggling, and it does not require inferring anything from percentages: zero means comfortable, anything sustained above it means the container is spending its life waiting for pages.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 9
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "showLegend": true,
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "range": true,
          "expr": "rate(container_pressure_memory_stalled_seconds_total{name=~\"crypto-alerts-.*\"}[5m]) > 0",
          "legendFormat": "{{name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
